-- title:
--   Regularity at affine places forces membership in the coordinate ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ (the Galois field `GaloisField q 2`), and assume that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q κ`, the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`, is a domain; write $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` for its fraction field. Let $C$ be a subgroup of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, and let [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) be the intermediate field of $F/\kappa$ fixed by the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `hFunctionFieldAction q κ ⟨(1, ζ)⟩` for $\zeta \in C$. Let $E$ be a field over $\kappa$, let $e : E \simeq$ `quotField q κ C` be an isomorphism of $\kappa$-algebras, and let $z \in E$. Assume that $z$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $Q$ of $E$ over $\kappa$ — that is, every valuation subring of $E$ that contains the image of $\kappa$, is not all of $E$, and is a principal ideal ring — with the property that $e^{-1}(w)$ lies in that valuation subring for every $w$ in `quotField q κ C` whose image in $F$ is $\mathrm{algebraMap}(c)$ for some $c \in$ `CoordRing q κ`. Then the image of $e(z)$ in $F$ lies in the range of the structure map `CoordRing q κ →` $F$.
--
--   This is the transport, along an abstract $\kappa$-isomorphism $E \cong F^C$, of the statement that a function on the quotient Drinfeld curve which is regular at every affine place lies in the coordinate ring. It is used in the analysis of the stalks at smooth points of the affine charts of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve, in the supersingular residue characteristic cases.
